WEBVTT

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.000
Maman was an expert at making jams.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.050
The raspberry jam was like a dream:

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.880
sweet and tart, and with a scent of grass.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.930
Papa, Grandfather, Grandmother, and my little brother, Jean...

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.270
They all loved Maman's jam.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:48.650
When spring came, the buds on the trees
would swell and rain would fall on the vineyards.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.780
The rays of the summer sun were bright...

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.990
and when the wheat harvest was complete,

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.740
the mountains became bright red, as if they were on fire.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:01.200
The snow was a gift from the angels.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.880
Yes, that's what my house was like.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:14.130
But... maybe the chimney was a little bigger.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:29.860
Am I boring you?

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.610
No, please tell me more.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.150
I want to know more and understand you, Cossette.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.600
Thank you.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.730
"In the way of a cavalier"...

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.980
My father was a wonderful gentleman,

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.190
with sky-blue eyes and a chestnut beard.

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.690
He always had a lit pipe...

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.990
with purple fragrant smoke.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:22.370
The purple was the color of blueberries.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:24.830
I love blueberries.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.120
Good evening.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:35.880
Marcello...

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.470
They say blueberries are one of the forest fairies' favorite foods.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.600
I always believed that.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.230
Marcello Orlando... What kind of person was he?

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.320
You draw really well, Eiri.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.420
Yuu...

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:14.920
Eiri!

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.300
Thank goodness!

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.260
I suddenly felt that you were going to disappear.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.480
Mataki...

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.610
Kurahashi...

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:41.070
What are you doing?!

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:56.500
<i>Theres no mistake...</i>

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.960
<i>It's wandering around the Zendouji Arcade Mall.</i>

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.840
<i>And at its center is...</i>

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.010
<i>Kourandou...</i>

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:11.180
I suddenly had a bad premonition, and couldn't help myself.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.940
Well, I'll believe you.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:17.480
I don't know about you, Kurahashi, but since Yuu says so...

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.570
Still, that's a surprise.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.990
I didn't think Yuu's sixth sense would catch it...

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.950
What about Yuu?

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:27.620
Just talking to myself. By the way, what'd you come here for?

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.410
Oh. By the way...

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.330
I wanted to show this to you as soon as I could.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.510
I tried looking up this artist.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.590
Then I found out that he has something of a cult following.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:50.390
Marcello Orlando... Date of birth unknown.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.180
An Italian painter of the 18th century.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.310
Exhibited talent in portraiture,

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.360
and received the patronage of the
d'Auvergne family during his stay in France.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:02.820
Painted numerous portraits of
the d'Auvergnes' daughter, Cossette.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.530
Portraits of Cossette...

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:10.490
Later on, he disappeared around the
time of the d'Auvergne family's demise.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.500
I'm strangely curious about him.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.750
Me too. He's unrefined, but still talented.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:21.670
Theres something in his paintings that speaks to the viewer.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:27.180
That too... But Kurahashi,
your art style's changed recently, hasn't it?

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:31.640
It's beyond what you could call replicas;
it's totally like you <i>are</i> him.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.100
I wasn't trying to copy his paintings...

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:38.060
What's this? You don't need to
imitate his signature too, you know.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.270
Weird... I don't remember writing anything like that.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.280
Mataki, could you go home soon?

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:51.830
Sorry.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.080
Hmph, what's up with him? That idiot.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.540
Shouko?

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:03.880
Cossette!

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:08.760
Cossette!

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.680
I want to ask you something, Cossette!

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:25.320
"To Cossette d'Auvergne. With love, Marcello Orlando."

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.240
When did I write something like this?

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.870
Marcello... Why does he interest me?

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.960
<i>I met the spirit of a girl</i>

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:44.880
<i>and inherited the soul and the fate of the man who killed her.</i>

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.680
<i>Even I know it's a crazy thing to
have done, but it's good in its own way...</i>

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:57.930
<i>After all, I've fallen in love with her, and it's what she wanted.</i>

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:00.940
<i>But...</i>

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.410
But why me, when there are billions of people in this world?

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.080
Besides who is Marcello...?

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.660
Eiri, you really <i>are</i> good at drawing.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.790
Cossette! Where are you?

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.460
Cossette...?

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:10.920
But I'm not very fond of having my portrait drawn, actually.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.880
What? What do you mean by that?

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:15.180
I don't like it.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:16.430
You don't like it?

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:20.850
But there are so many portraits of you... What about those?

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.270
Say, Cossette...

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.020
What kind of person was Marcello?

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:33.780
You didn't mention him in any of your stories, but as
far as I can tell from the portraits, you two were very...

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:41.200
Don't mention that name ever again.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.090
Cossette...

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.230
Why?

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:14.740
Is this the look of someone who doesn't want to be drawn?

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.620
We haven't seen Eiri around lately.

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.750
Haven't seen him in practical training, either.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.040
Is he even coming to class?

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:29.000
I saw him the other day.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:33.550
He was kind of out of it,
walking around town and talking to himself.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:37.180
Wha? Isn't that bad? Maybe he's holed himself up.

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:38.760
Hey, s-so what's the deal, Mataki?

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:42.600
He's just working. He goes straight to
that antique store first thing in the morning.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:48.650
Nah. It's a woman. He got a girlfriend.

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:49.730
Here we go!

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:53.230
Hisamoto-senpai's "girlfriend" theory!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:54.360
So, who is it?

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:59.200
I'd like to say it's Mataki, but well,
that'd have a 99% chance of being wrong–

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.200
Senpai!

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.830
It costs 1200 yen per dish at a
restaurant that serves sushi on a rotating belt!

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:03.910
Whoa, for real?!

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:05.790
That'd be 99% wrong.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:06.750
You think so?

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.460
So, it <i>is</i> about a girl?

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:09.730
<i>I thought I'd be able to see what it is...</i>

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:26.620
Ophthalmology

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:26.620
Great People with

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:26.620
Pretty Teeth

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.490
Oh stop it, Ms. Zenshinni.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.580
Aren't you seeking counsel from the wrong person?

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:30.000
Though I'm just a private practitioner,
I'm still a scientist of sorts.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.880
Even if you tell me that you see signs
of imminent death in Kurahashi's face...

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:37.630
I want to ask you <i>because</i> you're a scientist.
What do you think, Doctor?

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:43.180
What do <i>I</i> think? Well, I think that he's lost
some weight and he doesn't look well lately, but...

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:44.640
Is that all?

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:47.060
At this rate, he'll... die.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:51.060
That's ridiculous. Don't say such things just based on a whim.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.150
Is science omnipotent?

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:59.900
Is your sixth sense omnipotent?

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:02.280
He's not here?

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.280
Kurahashi isn't here?

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:06.740
That's right.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:08.950
Oh, don't mind me.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:12.210
It's a thank-you gift for always looking after me.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:19.130
Oh! Hey, Miss Michiru, about Kurahashi...

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.720
I was just reading his fortune.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:24.840
Oh, I see.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.510
Mr. Kurahashi is in love.

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:29.100
Love? Really?!

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:31.180
A love he's risking his life on, at that.

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.480
Risking his life on? Who is the girl?

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.190
Is it Yuu, after all?

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.110
Who knows... I can't tell who the girl is.

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:41.530
But I don't see anything like that
between them when I see them every day.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.150
Then, who?

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:46.530
More importantly, where'd he go?

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:02.050
The artist and his model seem like they are
deeply in love with each other, don't they?

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:05.590
Let's not look at such things.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:07.390
Cossette...

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.850
You cannot escape, Eiri.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:14.560
After all, you have made the pact of blood.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:16.560
You are mine, Eiri.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:20.610
I have no wish to escape... I just want to know.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:21.690
Know what?

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:26.610
You don't dislike being drawn... Actually, it makes you happy.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:30.410
Who was Marcello to you?

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.200
You shouldn't think of such needless things.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:38.040
Those antiques come from
beyond to seek revenge on you, Eiri.

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:42.710
You just need to tolerate suffering
without thinking about anything, Eiri.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.630
Cossette... but I want to know...

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:48.180
I want to know why I was chosen by you.

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:50.720
I want to know who Marcello is!

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:01.110
<i>I am just... to tolerate suffering...</i>

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.270
I smell apples.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:39.100
I tried apple tea today.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:41.900
It's very delicious.

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:44.230
I'm glad you like it.

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:47.860
You live in a nice place.

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:49.700
It brings peace to one's heart.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:51.780
I'm glad you like it.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:57.000
Back then, I was a naive child.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:02.170
I believed that the world was a
candy land, made of happiness and hope.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:06.050
I'm not a child anymore, but I still believe that.

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:08.510
Oh... is that so?

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:17.310
Sotilis? There you are, Sotilis!

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:19.350
Come here, Sotilis!

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:41.290
Cossette...

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:42.580
Don't touch me.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:04.900
Yes... My family members and I
were killed on that day, in this house.

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:09.070
The world wasn't made of happiness and hope.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:12.700
Marcello... Did he also then, too?

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.870
I said, don't mention that name again.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:18.450
I'm probably jealous... of him...

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:23.080
The smile you have in his paintings,
and his loving brush strokes...

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:25.750
So I can't help myself–

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:31.010
Do you want to know about him that much?

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:31.630
Yeah.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:34.760
About the man who killed me?

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:42.350
Th-That's... That's impossible.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.100
Then... if that's true, that painting...

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:54.200
Then, Marcello is within me...

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.620
You wished to know one more thing, didn't you?

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:02.040
I will tell you why I chose you.

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:07.380
You are a talented painter, and you love me.

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:10.420
It's because you're the same as Marcello.

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:13.050
Marcello...

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:14.840
was my fiancé.

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:17.430
Wh-What did you say?

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:19.470
You don't believe me?

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.890
But it's true.

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:26.350
He loved me, and I loved him very much.

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:27.690
Yet, he...

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:33.360
Can you understand the grief–
the sorrow of being killed by the one you love?

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.860
Can you understand my despair at learning

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:40.330
that what I'd thought was a pure sugar
confection... was a rotten lump of meat?

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:41.240
Yes...

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.700
How could you possibly understand?

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:46.080
Because you are Marcello, Eiri.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.130
How could he have killed you, even though he loved you?

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.800
Why don't you see it with your own eyes?

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:59.890
He should be killing me right about now.

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:25.750
I am...

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:27.000
Marcello?

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:32.670
Oh wow, what a great donation.

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:36.510
I guess it's no surprise that the memorial service of the
chairman of a large corporation would be something different.

00:18:58.570 --> 00:18:59.950
<i>It's the same smell...</i>

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:06.500
<i>Eiri... you are Marcello.</i>

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:09.330
<i>You are the one who killed me.</i>

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:21.840
<i>Yes... what you did was seen by the
glasses, the clock and many other things...</i>

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:28.020
<i>They hated you with such a violent passion
that in the end they harbored a demon within.</i>

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:33.400
<i>And their hatred entrapped my soul,</i>

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:36.900
<i>compelling me to wander this world alone until today.</i>

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:43.530
<i>You must atone for your sin.</i>

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:48.580
<i>Patiently endure the pain of having
your body gouged and torn asunder.</i>

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:03.930
<i>I will carve out and purify the souls of the antiques,
which have possessed you in order to kill you.</i>

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:14.900
<i>That... is the only waif in which I
ma escape to an eternal slumber</i>

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:27.580
<i>The same... as Marcello?</i>

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:30.750
<i>Someday I will think the same things he did...</i>

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:32.120
<i>and kill Cossette...</i>

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:41.130
<i>Why... Why must I endure such things?</i>

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:45.220
<i>Do I have to keep suffering such pain?</i>

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:05.030
Kurahashi? You're here, right, Kurahashi?

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:09.240
Today, I'll definitely make you
tell me everything, every last detail!

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:12.870
What have you been doing lately
that you're not telling anyone about?

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:16.420
Spit it out already, Kurahashi! Kurahashi–

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.170
Kurahashi?

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:23.260
Wh-What are you doing over there?

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:33.020
I... I don't know either...! I have no idea what I'm doing!

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:39.610
I-In any case, you have to get changed.

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:42.650
I'll go buy some clothes for you to
change into, so get out of those quickly.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.320
You'll get sick if you stay wet.

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:50.990
What is that...?

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.580
<i>How could I say anything...?</i>

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.880
<i>Even if I did, no one would believe me.</i>

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:10.220
What is it, Ms. Zenshinni? You said
you wanted to show me something...

00:22:10.220 --> 00:22:10.970
That.

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:23.570
I-It can't be... That's...!

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:43.590
<i>Just as I'd thought, the evil spirits that were
gathering at the shopping arcade were targeting him!</i>

00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:48.380
Kurahashi? Where are you? Kurahashi!

00:22:52.510 --> 00:22:55.350
<i>I'm sorry, Kurahashi. This is a drastic measure,</i>

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:59.690
<i>but I have no other way to force this
thing out of hiding and sever the bad karma!</i>

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:09.240
If you sincerely desire for the bodhisattva's
deliverance, you will not drown beneath the waves.

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:21.580
<i>My Buddhist chants are powerless!</i>

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:49.740
Cossette...!

00:25:07.110 --> 00:25:11.900
O cursed antique, let your soul now rest in sleep eternal.

00:25:30.630 --> 00:25:31.800
You must not move.

00:25:33.090 --> 00:25:34.380
Please don't move.

00:25:34.420 --> 00:25:36.930
You do not have the right to disobey me.

00:25:36.930 --> 00:25:37.680
No...

00:25:38.180 --> 00:25:41.640
Why... why must <i>I</i> tolerate suffering?

00:25:41.640 --> 00:25:45.940
To atone for your sin. You have that responsibility.

00:25:45.940 --> 00:25:48.060
I am not the one who committed this sin!

00:25:48.100 --> 00:25:50.690
It is you. You are Marcello.

00:25:50.690 --> 00:25:53.030
I don't care... about that!

00:26:03.080 --> 00:26:04.870
<i>I don't want to... die!</i>

00:26:08.170 --> 00:26:11.340
<i>I don't want to lose... the light of life...</i>

00:26:12.550 --> 00:26:15.630
<i>and the bright... future...!</i>

00:26:28.310 --> 00:26:30.360
<i>This... sensation is...</i>

00:27:23.870 --> 00:27:25.580
M-Marcello...

00:27:25.580 --> 00:27:27.000
Wh-Why?

00:27:27.290 --> 00:27:31.080
My dear Cossette... why are you trying to become an adult?

00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:38.130
My paintings are crystallizations of
beauty that even God Himself would marvel at.

00:27:38.130 --> 00:27:41.930
And yet if you, the model, changes, it's no good.

00:27:42.680 --> 00:27:43.890
M-Marcello...!

00:27:43.890 --> 00:27:45.970
You must not change.

00:27:46.510 --> 00:27:50.440
You should continue to appear the
way you do in my paintings forever.

00:27:54.690 --> 00:27:55.730
Don't worry.

00:27:57.610 --> 00:27:59.110
I will stop your time...

00:28:00.110 --> 00:28:01.780
so that you...

00:28:03.320 --> 00:28:04.370
will remain beautiful.

00:28:10.040 --> 00:28:11.000
Why...

00:28:11.410 --> 00:28:13.080
Why me?

00:28:14.960 --> 00:28:16.340
But I love you!

00:28:17.050 --> 00:28:19.670
I love you too, Cossette...

00:28:56.420 --> 00:28:58.170
Cossette... do it.

00:29:03.760 --> 00:29:04.930
Hurry...!

00:29:10.350 --> 00:29:12.310
Hurry!!

00:29:41.670 --> 00:29:43.010
Stop!

00:30:12.080 --> 00:30:14.040
<i>I love Cossette.</i>

00:30:14.620 --> 00:30:17.670
<i>Just like Marcello did, with a strong and single-minded love.</i>

00:30:18.040 --> 00:30:20.170
<i>But, I am different from him.</i>

00:30:20.590 --> 00:30:23.880
<i>No matter how extreme the suffering,
I can endure it for Cossette's sake!</i>

00:30:32.140 --> 00:30:33.140
<i>Eiri...</i>

00:30:50.530 --> 00:30:52.740
<i>Why was I sleeping in a place like this?</i>

00:30:57.080 --> 00:30:58.790
<i>What is that?</i>

00:31:20.940 --> 00:31:21.940
Eiri...

00:31:25.110 --> 00:31:26.320
Back then...

00:31:27.530 --> 00:31:30.910
when the suffering was too much
to bear, and I grasped your shoulder,

00:31:31.780 --> 00:31:33.870
I was stunned at how thin it was.

00:31:36.410 --> 00:31:39.460
Almost painfully slender and delicate...

00:31:39.460 --> 00:31:41.580
as though it could break at any instant...

00:31:46.340 --> 00:31:51.090
You've endured solitude and despair
in that small body of yours until today.

00:31:51.800 --> 00:31:54.350
But you're no longer all alone.

00:31:55.560 --> 00:31:56.430
Eiri...

00:32:16.580 --> 00:32:17.790
You're warm.

00:32:19.040 --> 00:32:20.000
Cossette...

00:32:39.640 --> 00:32:43.310
Just... who... <i>Who</i> could you fall in love with...

00:32:44.150 --> 00:32:45.770
that'd make you end up like that...

00:32:46.360 --> 00:32:47.360
Kurahashi?!

00:33:06.130 --> 00:33:09.960
<i>Who would love me so much that he would cast aside</i>

00:33:10.000 --> 00:33:12.300
<i>his own precious life?</i>

00:33:13.260 --> 00:33:13.970
<i>Is it you?</i>

00:33:22.810 --> 00:33:27.190
Listening quietly to the singing

00:33:27.270 --> 00:33:33.190
that secretly flows down my way,

00:33:34.070 --> 00:33:38.450
we share the white sigh of the moon

00:33:38.530 --> 00:33:44.330
with a sweet kiss

00:33:45.410 --> 00:33:50.380
as though we're lovers.

00:33:50.880 --> 00:33:53.760
Hold me closer.

00:33:53.840 --> 00:33:57.590
I feel as though my love is supported

00:33:57.760 --> 00:34:03.930
by the depth of the wounds I must atone for.

00:34:04.230 --> 00:34:08.850
So for now, I want to thaw your frozen heart

00:34:08.940 --> 00:34:15.780
with pain, rather than kindness.

00:34:16.280 --> 00:34:20.160
I will always be close to you

00:34:20.240 --> 00:34:26.290
like a shadow you cannot elude.

00:34:26.620 --> 00:34:31.290
The teardrops you let fall

00:34:31.840 --> 00:34:39.550
adorn my fingers like jewels, shining brightly.

00:35:04.160 --> 00:35:07.750
We will surely go together

00:35:08.000 --> 00:35:14.170
beyond these meadows that glisten so brilliantly.

00:35:14.460 --> 00:35:19.090
So for now, I will cling to the strength of our entwined fingers,

00:35:19.430 --> 00:35:25.970
and not let go of your solitude

00:35:26.560 --> 00:35:30.350
because we will be able to find

00:35:30.560 --> 00:35:36.570
the flicker of light, even deep in the darkness.

00:35:36.820 --> 00:35:41.700
Searching for the distant jeweled slumber,

00:35:41.990 --> 00:35:50.080
I have faith in the strength to go beyond the night.
